-# R0dump Manager Design System
-
-## Visual Direction
-
-Android 16 system configuration tool using Jetpack Compose, Material 3 Expressive, dynamic color, edge-to-edge layout, and standard system typography. Design serves repeated operational work: compact, familiar, and state-driven.
-
-## Color
-
-- Prefer Android dynamic color in light and dark themes.
-- Fallback primary: `#465D91` light, `#AFC6FF` dark.
-- Fallback surface: `#FAF8FF` light, `#121318` dark.
-- Success is reserved for verified completion; enabled sessions use primary state styling.
-- Warning and error colors communicate dirty, interrupted, invalid, or costly states, never decoration.
-
-## Typography
-
-- Use the platform Material 3 typography and Roboto family.
-- App title: bold `titleLarge`; page title: bold `titleLarge`; section and group titles: bold `titleMedium`.
-- Body labels: `bodyLarge` or `bodyMedium`.
-- Masks, descriptors, and byte values use monospace where scanning benefits. Internal run IDs and generations are not exposed in the primary UI.
-- Do not use display typography inside compact tool surfaces.
-
-## Shape And Elevation
-
-- Content groups and cards use at most 8 dp corner radius.
-- Use standard Material component shapes for fields and buttons.
-- Do not nest cards.
-- Elevation is limited to persistent action surfaces, sheets, and dialogs.
-
-## Spacing And Sizing
-
-- Spacing scale: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, and 32 dp.
-- Compact horizontal padding: 16 dp; medium: 24 dp; expanded: 32 dp.
-- List rows are at least 56 dp and touch targets at least 48 dp.
-- Toolbars, buttons, counters, and loading states keep stable dimensions.
-
-## Layout
-
-- Compact: top app bar with language, refresh, and capture-state switch actions, a single scrolling column, contextual secondary actions, and four-item bottom navigation.
-- Medium: navigation rail, single content column, and contextual docked actions.
-- Expanded: navigation rail and a centered editing column up to 720 dp.
-- Insets are consumed once by the root scaffold; action surfaces must not cover the final form row.
-
-## Components
-
-- Capture state: the top-right switch is the only persistent enabled/disabled signal. Run IDs, generations, and duplicate device-state text remain internal unless an error requires recovery.
-- The switch keeps a 48 dp semantic touch target while its visual control is scaled down for the compact TopAppBar.
-- Capture state: the top-right switch is the primary enable/disable action; authentication success continues the pending transition without a second tap.
-- Contextual actions: refresh lives in the TopAppBar. A valid draft transition shows one short native Toast and exposes publish-only as a compact TopAppBar icon after authentication. The bottom action surface is reserved for validation errors and recovery state; it never persists a generic "draft changed" banner.
-- Validation feedback: the contextual error surface names each affected field and gives its localized correction, shows up to three issues without taking over the screen, and directs users to inline highlighted fields when more remain.
-- Manager-owned fields such as run ID are repaired or generated automatically and never presented as user-fixable validation errors.
-- Booleans use switches, capture points use checkboxes inside expandable category headers, enums use segmented controls or chips, and numeric values use text fields with units.
-- Capture point category headers show selected and total counts. All groups start collapsed on first use, then restore the user's latest expanded/collapsed choices.
-- Capture point rows lead with the actual ART or libcore source function. The stable runtime point ID remains visible as secondary text so operators can correlate the selection with logs and artifacts.
-- Budgets use two expandable groups, capacity limits and records/flushing, with the same header, summary, chevron, and motion vocabulary as advanced settings. Reset is an icon action beside the page title rather than a full-width trailing button.
-- Notification permission is explained only when the user starts a capture without notifications enabled; it does not occupy persistent page space.
-- Advanced settings use three expandable headers for Manifest, Walk, and Force/ANR; headers summarize enabled state and validation errors reveal hidden fields. ANR protection is the first control inside Force/ANR so its independent session policy is visible before force-invoke selectors.
-- The selected destination and expanded/collapsed state of capture, budget, and advanced groups persist across activity and process recreation. Transient menus and search activation do not persist.
-- Walk start and mode use full-width Material 3 dropdown fields; the closed field shows the current value and the open menu marks the current item.
-- The Apps destination starts with the primary "Application selection" title followed immediately by application search; it does not repeat a description or insert an empty spacer.
-- Icon-only buttons require content descriptions and tooltips where the icon is not universally familiar.
-
-## Motion
-
-Use Material 3 expressive motion only for state feedback, typically 150 to 250 ms. Capture groups, advanced groups, and additional budgets animate height and opacity when expanded or collapsed; dropdown menus use the Material transition. No decorative page entrances, bouncing, pulsing, or transaction logic that depends on animation completion. Reduced motion falls back to crossfade or instant state changes.
-
-## Localization
-
-English and Simplified Chinese are equal layout targets. Technical identifiers remain unchanged. Every screenshot pass covers both languages, all four destinations, important enabled/disabled/error states, and portrait/landscape layouts.
-
-## Visual Verification
-
-- Use screenshots from the physical OnePlus 9 as the primary visual evidence; emulator or preview captures are supplemental only.
-- Capture each iteration in both English and Simplified Chinese for the session, capture points, budgets, and advanced destinations.
-- Cover unauthenticated disabled, authenticated disabled, enabled, validation-error, and in-flight states where applicable.
-- Verify portrait and landscape at the physical display size, then exercise at least one medium or expanded window configuration.
-- Inspect every capture for text truncation, overlap, hidden final rows, unstable control dimensions, insufficient contrast, and touch targets smaller than 48 dp.
-- Store captures with descriptive names containing the destination, state, locale, and orientation so before/after comparisons remain reproducible.
-- End each verification pass with the device in a disabled session state and confirm that the target process and active-session notification are absent.
-
-The normative UI/UX requirements remain sections 8 and 10 of [IMPLEMENTATION.md](IMPLEMENTATION.md).
+# R0dump Manager 设计系统
+
+## 视觉方向
+
+采用 Jetpack Compose、Material 3 Expressive、动态取色、edge-to-edge 布局和系统标准字体，
+形成 Android 16 系统配置工具。设计服务于重复操作，应紧凑、熟悉并以状态为中心。
+
+## 颜色
+
+- 浅色和深色主题优先使用 Android 动态取色。
+- 浅色后备主色：`#465D91`；深色后备主色：`#AFC6FF`。
+- 浅色后备 surface：`#FAF8FF`；深色后备 surface：`#121318`。
+- success 色只表示已验证完成；启用中的会话使用主色状态样式。
+- warning 和 error 色只表达草稿、异常中断、无效或高成本状态，不作装饰。
+
+## 字体
+
+- 使用平台 Material 3 typography 和 Roboto 字体族。
+- 应用标题和页面标题使用加粗 `titleLarge`；分区和分组标题使用加粗 `titleMedium`。
+- 正文标签使用 `bodyLarge` 或 `bodyMedium`。
+- mask、descriptor 和字节值在有利于扫描时使用等宽字体。主界面不展示内部 run ID 和 generation，
+  除非错误恢复确实需要。
+- 紧凑工具界面不使用 display 级大字号。
+
+## 形状与层级
+
+- 内容分组和卡片的圆角不超过 8 dp。
+- 输入框和按钮使用标准 Material 组件形状。
+- 不嵌套卡片。
+- elevation 只用于常驻操作面、sheet 和 dialog。
+
+## 间距与尺寸
+
+- 间距刻度：4、8、12、16、24、32 dp。
+- compact 水平边距为 16 dp，medium 为 24 dp，expanded 为 32 dp。
+- 列表行至少 56 dp，触控目标至少 48 dp。
+- toolbar、按钮、计数器和加载状态保持稳定尺寸。
+
+## 布局
+
+- Compact：顶部应用栏包含语言、刷新和捕获状态开关；主体为单列滚动内容，带上下文次要操作和四项底部导航。
+- Medium：使用 navigation rail、单列内容和停靠式上下文操作区。
+- Expanded：使用 navigation rail，编辑列居中且最大宽度为 720 dp。
+- 根 Scaffold 只消费一次 inset；操作区不得遮住表单最后一行。
+
+## 组件
+
+- 右上角开关是唯一常驻的捕获启用/禁用信号。run ID、generation 和重复设备状态默认保持内部化，
+  只有错误恢复需要时才显示。
+- 开关保留 48 dp 语义触控目标，compact TopAppBar 中仅缩小视觉控件。
+- 开关是主要启停操作，点击后直接继续待处理状态转换。
+- 刷新位于 TopAppBar。有效草稿转换只显示一次短 Toast；可在 TopAppBar 提供紧凑的“仅发布”图标。
+  底部操作面只用于校验错误和恢复状态，不常驻“草稿已修改”横幅。
+- 校验错误区必须指出受影响字段和本地化修正方式，最多直接展示三项；更多错误引导到行内高亮字段。
+- Manager 管理的 run ID 等字段自动修复或生成，不显示为需要用户处理的错误。
+- 布尔值使用 switch，捕获点使用可展开分类内的 checkbox，枚举使用 segmented control 或 chip，
+  数值使用带单位的输入框。
+- 捕获点分类标题显示已选数和总数。首次使用时默认折叠，后续恢复用户最近的展开状态。
+- 捕获点行首先显示真实 ART/libcore 源函数；稳定 runtime point ID 作为次要文本保留，便于关联日志和产物。
+- 预算分为“容量限制”和“数量/刷新”两个可展开组，与高级设置共用标题、摘要、箭头和动效语言。
+  重置使用页面标题旁的图标操作，不使用底部通栏按钮。
+- 只有用户在通知未启用时启动捕获，才解释通知权限；不占用常驻页面空间。
+- 高级设置分为 Manifest、Walk、Force/ANR 三个可展开组。标题汇总启用状态，校验错误自动展开隐藏字段。
+  ANR protection 位于 Force/ANR 组首项，以便先展示其独立会话策略。
+- 当前页面、捕获/预算/高级分组的展开状态在 Activity 和进程重建后保留；临时菜单和搜索激活状态不保留。
+- Walk 启动方式和模式使用全宽 Material 3 下拉框；闭合时显示当前值，展开菜单标记当前项。
+- Apps 页面首先显示“应用选择”，随后直接显示搜索，不重复说明或插入空白占位。
+- 纯图标按钮必须有内容描述；图标含义不通用时还需 tooltip。
+
+## 动效
+
+Material 3 Expressive 动效只用于状态反馈，通常为 150 到 250 ms。捕获组、高级组和附加预算组展开/折叠时
+只改变高度和透明度；下拉菜单使用 Material 标准过渡。禁止装饰性页面入场、弹跳、脉冲，以及依赖动画完成的
+事务逻辑。减少动态效果时退化为 crossfade 或即时变化。
+
+## 本地化
+
+英文和简体中文是同等布局目标，技术标识保持原样。每轮截图覆盖两种语言、四个页面、重要的启用/禁用/错误状态，
+以及横竖屏布局。
+
+## 视觉验收
+
+- 以 OnePlus 9 真机截图作为主要视觉证据；模拟器或 Preview 只作补充。
+- 每轮覆盖英文和简体中文的会话、捕获点、预算和高级设置页面。
+- 按适用情况覆盖 owner-only、已启用、校验错误和执行中状态。
+- 先检查真机分辨率下的横竖屏，再检查至少一种 medium 或 expanded 窗口。
+- 检查文字截断、控件重叠、末行遮挡、尺寸跳动、对比度不足和小于 48 dp 的触控目标。
+- 截图文件名包含页面、状态、语言和方向，确保前后对比可复现。
+- 每轮结束时设备必须处于禁用会话状态，并确认目标进程和活动会话通知均不存在。
+
+UI/UX 的规范正文仍以 [IMPLEMENTATION.md](IMPLEMENTATION.md) 第 8、10 章为准。
